# door-handwritten.dl6 -- text-door receipt program, and the served engine's
# receipt (a) program (plans/2026-07-29-runtime-bridge-header.md scope 4a).
#
# REPAIRED 2026-07-29 (runtime bridge arc). The rule used to read
#
#   current(Id, Kind) <- latest(event(Id, Kind)).
#
# and that spelling COMPILES NOWHERE at HEAD: `latest_in_level_rule` refuses it
# in a level rule (the review-B2 refusal), and `edge_body_with_latest` refuses
# the `<+` form too. Both refusals landed after this file was written and
# nothing gated it, so the checked-in emitted module went stale in silence. The
# rule is now the plain level rule; `latest`'s missing compiling form is the
# open review finding A12/B1 (lower latest as the negation path minus NOT
# EXISTS), not something this file works around.

rel result(ok(value: text) ; error(message: text)).
rel event(id: int, kind: text) log keep(all).
rel current(id: int, kind: text).

current(Id, Kind) <- event(Id, Kind).
